From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] FP6: manual exposure/gain/EV/white balance, long exposures

Self-contained FP6 addition, applied after all other camera-fp6-pmos
patches (keep it last; rebase when the soft IPA changes):

* ipa/simple/fp6_manual.{h,cpp} (new): AeEnable, ExposureTimeMode,
  ExposureTime, AnalogueGainMode, AnalogueGain, ExposureValue, AwbEnable,
  ColourGains, ColourTemperature. Applied in processStats() after the
  regular algorithms, so full auto at EV 0 is untouched. Manual exposure
  times beyond the default frame length extend V4L2_CID_VBLANK up to the
  sensor maximum (frame rate drops accordingly); auto always runs at the
  default frame length. ExposureValue drives the Agc's evFactor (0021);
  with only one of exposure/gain manual the other follows the Agc's
  correction (0021). Reports ExposureTimeMode, AnalogueGainMode,
  AeEnable, ExposureValue, AwbEnable, ColourTemperature (manual),
  FrameDuration and FrameDurationLimits metadata.
* pipeline/simple + soft IPA: the IPA gets the configured sensor mode
  (IPAConfigInfo.sensorInfo) so its line duration matches the running
  mode; it was taken from the mode at camera creation (on the IMX896 the
  full-resolution line, 18 % too long, whenever a previous session left
  that mode set).
* pipeline/simple: VBLANK in DelayedControls (priority write, before
  EXPOSURE), and VBLANK reset to the mode default when a session is
  configured.
* gstreamer: libcamerasrc also exposes ColourTemperature, AfTrigger,
  AfState, FrameDuration and FrameDurationLimits; its control lists are
  accessed under the state lock (set_property raced queueRequest and
  requestCompleted), and pending controls are attached to a request only
  once it has its buffers (a request dropped for lack of buffers took the
  controls with it, so most controls set while streaming were lost).

---
